The thing that helped me most was learning to pace myself.

Spend more time on the first dungeon level, and the second. Going down
real fast is a problem, as monsters get tougher (on average) very quickly.

Make sure your experience level is high enough... but don't wait too long that
you die of hunger.

Yes, that's a tough balancing act.  But rushing into things unless you're
a very experienced player is a bad idea.


